      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Mientras tanto, caminaba por el mundo Kvasir, el ser nacido de la saliva de la paz entre los dioses.",
          "en": "Meanwhile, Kvasir walked the world, the being born from the spit of the peace between the gods."
        },
        {
          "es": "Era tan sabio que podía responder cualquier pregunta, y enseñaba a los hombres lo que sabía.",
          "en": "He was so wise that he could answer any question, and he taught people what he knew."
        },
        {
          "es": "Un día, dos enanos, Fjalar y Galar, lo invitaron a hablar a solas, y lo mataron.",
          "en": "One day two dwarves, Fjalar and Galar, invited him to talk in private, and killed him."
        },
        {
          "es": "Dejaron correr su sangre en dos vasijas y una caldera, y la mezclaron con miel.",
          "en": "They let his blood run into two vats and a kettle, and mixed it with honey."
        },
        {
          "es": "Así nació un hidromiel mágico: quien lo bebía se volvía poeta y sabio.",
          "en": "Thus a magic mead was born: whoever drank it became a poet and a sage."
        }
      ],
